urn1search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: 13.0 years ago; Crawled: 4 months ago; # Cordial labeling of hypertrees ... Sylwia Cichacz ... Agnieszka Gorlich ... Zsolt Tuza ... Image: Request Full-text Paper PDF ... From our theorems it follows that every k-uniform hypertree is k-cordial, and every hypertree with n or m odd is 2-cordial.\nArticle\n\n# Cordial labeling of hypertrees\n\n  * November 2013\n  * Discrete Mathematics 313(22):2518–2524\n\nDOI:10.1016/j.disc.2013.07.025\n\nAuthors:\n\nSylwia Cichacz\n\n  * AGH University of Krakow\n\nAgnieszka Gorlich\n\nAgnieszka Gorlich\n\n  * This person is not on ResearchGate, or hasn't claimed this research yet.\n\nZsolt Tuza\n\n  * University of Pannonia\n\nImage: Request Full-text Paper PDF\n\nRequest full-text PDF\n\nTo read the full-text of this research, you can request a copy directly from the authors.\n\n## Abstract\n\nLet H = (V,E) be a hypergraph with vertex set V = {v_1,..., v_n} and edge set E = {e_1,...,e_m}. A vertex labeling c : V -> N induces an edge labeling c¤*: E -> N by the rule c*(e_i) =\\sum{v_j \\in e_i}c(v_j ). For integers k >1 we study the existence of labelings satisfying the following condition: Every residue class modulo k occurs exactly \\cell n\\k\\cell or \\floor n\\k \\floor times in the sequence c(v_1),...,c(v_n) and exactly \\cell m\\k \\cell or \\floor m\\k \\floor times in the sequence c*(e_1),...,c*(e_m). Hypergraph H is called k-cordial if it admits a labeling with these properties. Hovey [Discrete Math. 93 (1991), 183{194] raised the conjecture (still open for k > 5) that if H is a tree graph, then it is k-cordial for every k. Here we investigate the analogous problem for hypertrees (connected hypergraphs without cycles) and present various su±cient conditions on H to be k-cordial. From our theorems it follows that every k-uniform hypertree is k-cordial, and every hypertree with n or m odd is 2-cordial. Both of these results generalize Cahit's theorem [Ars Combin. 23 (1987), 201{207] which states that every tree graph is 2-cordial. We also prove that every uniform hyperpath is k-cordial for every k.\n\n\n## No full-text available\n\nImage: Request Full-text Paper PDF\n\nTo read the full-text of this research,\nyou can request a copy directly from the authors.\n\nRequest full-text PDF--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPublikacje - BaDAP AGH (https://badap.agh.edu.pl/publikacje?keywords_facets=hypertree)\nciteturn1search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 weeks ago; $Z_{2} × Z_{2}$-cordial cycle-free hypergraphs / Sylwia CICHACZ, Agnieszka GÖRLICH, Zsolt Tuza // Discussiones Mathematicae. ... Cordial labeling of hypertrees / Sylwia CICHACZ, Agnieszka GÖRLICH, Zsolt Tuza // Discrete Mathematics ; ISSN 0012-365X. — 2013 — vol. 313 iss. 22, s.\n\n# Wyszukiwarka publikacji\n\n  1. Strona główna/\n  2. Wyszukiwarka publikacji\n\n[Select]\n\nWyszukaj w opisie bibliograficznym\n\n[Input: Wyszukaj w opisie bibliograficznym]Szukaj\n\n## Wyniki wyszukiwania zapytania\n\nSzukaj wśród wyników[Input: Szukaj wśród wyników]Szukaj\n\nAutor\n\n[Input]Cichacz-Przeniosło Sylwia(2)\n\n[Input]Görlich Agnieszka(2)\n\n[Input]Tuza Zsolt(2)\n\nDyscyplina\n\n[Input]matematyka(1)\n\nJednostka\n\n[Input]WMS(2)\n\nRok publikacji\n\n[Input]2021(1)\n\n[Input]2013(1)\n\nTyp publikacji\n\n[Input]artykuły(2)\n\nCzasopismo\n\n[Input]Discrete Mathematics(1)\n\n[Input]Discussiones Mathematicae,...(1)\n\nSłowa kluczowe\n\n[Input]hypertree(2)\n\n[Input]hypergraph(2)\n\n[Input]V4 cordial graph(1)\n\n[Input]hypergraph labeling(1)\n\n[Input]k-cordial graph(1)\n\nWięcej 1\n\nPunktacja ministerialna\n\n[Input]Tak(2)\n\nIF/LF\n\n[Input]Tak(2)\n\nBazy referencyjne\n\n[Input]Web of Science(2)\n\nRecenzowane\n\n[Input]Tak(2)\n\nNaukowe\n\n[Input]Tak(2)\n\nOtwarty dostęp\n\n[Input]Nie(2)\n\nJęzyk publikacji\n\n[Input]angielski(2)\n\nSłowo kluczowe: hypertree\n\n(0/2)\n\nartykuł\n\n#134917 Data dodania: 5.7.2021\n\n$Z_{2} × Z_{2}$-cordial cycle-free hypergr